ere is having  a great time really enjoying themselves  and and you know in love with the music  and what they're doing um it's you know  it's just contagious and so i think  that's you know people can tell you have  such good energy like i just say i can  feel it coming from you how do you how  do you edc fans in vegas differ from  crowds in other cities like edc mexico  or uh in korea i know you've been there  indeed you've been all over the world  how do vegas fans differ um i mean i  think  you know vegas is is one thing and then  edc vegas i think is a whole nother  thing because  it's so notorious around the world  there's so many international fans who i  see here who maybe never have gotten to  see a nightmare show and this is their  first time getting to experience it so  it's cool seeing such a diverse crowd  and such a you know hearing languages  that i you know don't understand and  just people traveling from all over over  the world to to come to vegas to witness  this show so um but the energy is always  the same it's always super high energy  it's something you know i try to keep in  all of my shows now you're going to be  joined on stage by some special guest  can you give us some details on that  well this performance is um a kind of a  collaborative performance with a duo  called big gigantic and they're  incredibly talented musicians they  inspired me when i was first getting  into things and they're from colorado  and so yeah um dom and jeremy are the  two guys dom plays live drums and uh  jeremy or i mean uh jeremy plays live  drums dom will be playing saxophone keys  and occasionally we'll switch up djing  and stuff so it's cool this is a little  bit different more live music mixed with  electronic music kind of combination and  uh we've only done it two other three  other times ever so we're excited sounds  amazing i'm so excited so you have a new  single out which we were listening to  right before the show tell us a little  bit about that um so yeah this one i  wrote with my brother uh one of my  buddies clocks he's just a good friend  of mine we both went to um a music  school in la together um and uh yeah  it's just like a very  happy feel-good kind of energetic song  it's more of an easy listening song  definitely have some some songs of mine  that are not so relaxing and chill and  this is more in that lane so um it's  called the one and uh yeah i'm just just  really excited for that one to be out  when when you say you know relaxing what  do you do to relax i know you played  tennis as a kid do you still do you  still play tennis um i don't i honestly  don't play a ton of sports these days  i'm more into like i'm a hiker i'd  rather you know i go outside and uh you  know  try to hike by myself i feel like that's  kind of my moment of zen do you ever go  up to red rock i have done red rock a  bunch of times i love i love vegas mount  charleston i've done  you know you get the local badge you are  now how do you say nevada that's the  true test  do you say nevada or nevada oh gosh say  nevada nevada yes yeah you're local now  you are it is official thank you so much  for joining us thank you nightmare is  kicking off edc week at liquid tomorrow  and then edc where he will be performing  back to back with fellow dj and producer  big gigantic like we talked about as  gigantic nightmare at midnight at the  cosmic meadow stage  well

